{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/937294-high-ranking-death-spirits","id":937294,"title":"High-Ranking Death Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-25T14:31:45-07:00","id":937294,"title":"High-Ranking Death Spirits","content":"I was reading through some older posts here and was interested in what Seraph Kitty mentions here;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imperial Mysteries theorizes that the Deathlords are rank 7 or 8, each ruling over a type of death, and are possible exiled gods of Stygia. According to some of Dave B's posts on the subject, rank 7 are &quot;spirits of a species or tribal totems&quot;, rank 8 are spirits which &quot;rule a world, like Father Wolf, Luna, and Helios.&quot; So I'd guess the Horsemen to be the rank 7, and Death itself (if there is such an entity) to be rank 8. </div> </div> </div>I find Death-resonant Spirits really interesting in general and was interested to see that such powerful spirits as Luna and Helios would be Rank 8.<br /> <br /> My question is this; I'm sure a Rank 9 or 10 Death Spirit could be out there... With Rank 9 are we talking Exalted Primordials such as Gaia? What's a Rank 10 spirit and what would a Death resonant spirit be that had such a rank? If Death is Rank 8, what is Rank 9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:43:46-07:00","id":937302,"title":"","content":"I would think a being like Azrael from Terry Pratchett's Reaper Man, the Death of the Universe. It would be the thing which ferries the souls of dead stars and crushed planets to the Other Side. It is that which holds the Clock of Time, whose big hand only goes round one time and whose chime at 12 o'clock will ring out into the silence of the dead universe, when all energy is so dispersed as to be nonexistent for all practical purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:54:09-07:00","id":937307,"title":"","content":"Interesting... I'd think in that regard that something like Wraith's Oblivion could be a Rank 10 spirit in that regard then, when it comes to the death of Creation itself...<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a Rank 9 spirit bringing the death of worlds in said Universe...<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Rank 9 spirit being that large world-reaper spirit and Rank 10 being the force one may call Entropy and the inevitably of the heath-death itself. These are clearly things perhaps beyond a Geist game, though I do like the idea of a Rank 8 'Death personified' as a perhaps recurring entity...<br /> <br /> Any more thoughts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:00:12-07:00","id":937312,"title":"","content":"My <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/6512-a-theory-on-geist-advancement\">working model</a> is that &quot;deathlord&quot; is the chthonic Rank equivalent of &quot;Celestine,&quot; such that the Horsemen are Rank 8 and more particular deathlords are Rank 7; going off of the theory that Gaia is the spirit of the terrestrial Shadow, a Rank 9 chthonian would be Tartarus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:03:44-07:00","id":937315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/937294-high-ranking-death-spirits?p=937307#post937307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... I'd think in that regard that something like Wraith's Oblivion could be a Rank 10 spirit in that regard then, when it comes to the death of Creation itself...<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a Rank 9 spirit bringing the death of worlds in said Universe...<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Rank 9 spirit being that large world-reaper spirit and Rank 10 being the force one may call Entropy and the inevitably of the heath-death itself. These are clearly things perhaps beyond a Geist game, though I do like the idea of a Rank 8 'Death personified' as a perhaps recurring entity...<br /> <br /> Any more thoughts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, as far as I know, Rank 10 is basically God, an omnipotent being. Rank 9 would therefore be subdivisions of that totality, such as the opposing forces of entropy and order, with the Death of the Universe being a weaker Rank 9 ( as there is some variance within Ranks in terms of power).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T00:52:02-07:00","id":937507,"title":"","content":"In an old mage book, it had the primal wild being a rank 10 entity in its own right, but I think OP has decided to sweep that under the rug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T01:30:40-07:00","id":937513,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon, the Horsemen are the Rank 9 beings of the Underworld, as they represent the 5 Thresholds of Death. The very concept of death (simply known as &quot;Death&quot;) in the Rank 10 ruler of the Great Bellow, being represented as the Ocean of Fragments and all the Rivers who flow toward it (some sort of mirror to the Principle- one is the collective Divine Fire, while the other is the Water of the Dead).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/937294-high-ranking-death-spirits?p=937507#post937507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In an old mage book, it had the primal wild being a rank 10 entity in its own right, but I think OP has decided to sweep that under the rug.</div> </div> </div> </div>which book was it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com